 The publishing workflow verifies the signed APK and publishes both the checksum-named
 asset and the stable `bb-android.apk` alias, then `latest.json`.
+
+## Build-only native desktop staging
+
+In an owned source checkout, `BB_DESKTOP_STAGING=1 pnpm desktop:worktree --build-only` packages a native fixture without launching it. The build selects update services with no updater runtime imports. Automatic checks, manual checks, downloads, and installation are disabled even if runtime update flags are enabled. Packaging uses `dev.bb.qa.native-staging`, product `bb Native Staging`, and package/cache name `bb-native-staging`; it writes `apps/desktop/release-staging`, with no publish provider or update feed. Staging rejects publishing requests and mismatched build/package policy.
+
+Do not use `/Applications` as a staging target. Inspect the exact staged bundle and its updater exclusion before any separate launch. The staging build flag does not change normal release packaging when absent.
